Well, keep in mind that lujvo are their own words.  So I would guess that
{mamymamta} is defined something like: "x1 mamta x3 po'u mamta be x2".  So,
lujvo can mean stuff that isn't necessarily obvious from the rafsi involved
because they can be defined however you like.  Tanru on the other hand have
no problem because the relationship between the seltau and tertau is vague
so {broda broda} could mean any number of different things and the
"reasonable default assumption" will be different depending on what gismu
{broda} is.

